  "answer_text": "It looks like you're referring to **Iuka, Mississippi** (sometimes spelled \"Luka\")! Here's a quick overview:\n\n- **Iuka** (pronounced *eye-YOO-kuh*) is a city in and the county seat of **Tishomingo County, Mississippi**.\n\n- Its population was **3,139** at the 2020 census.\n\n- **Woodall Mountain**, the highest point in Mississippi, is located just south of Iuka.\n\n- Iuka is built on the site of a **Chickasaw village**, and the name \"Iuka\" comes from the name of one of the chiefs of that village.\n\n- The city was founded by **David Hubbard**, a wagon train scout, and Euro-American settlers arrived with the **Memphis and Charleston Railroad in 1857**.\n\n- The **Civil War** brought widespread devastation when a major engagement occurred on **September 19, 1862** \u2014 the **Battle of Iuka** \u2014 resulting in 1,200 to 1,500 killed or wounded.\n\n- Iuka is located in **northeast Mississippi**, with U.S. Route 72 running through the southern part of the city.\n\n- There is also a notable **Luka Springs** \u2014 a public drinking spring located in the area.\n\nIs there something specific about Iuka/Luka, Mississippi you'd like to know more about? \ud83d\ude0a",
